d test their phone connection before they call the interviewer.',40),(2296,42,167,NULL,166,41,'matching','It is annoying to the interviewer to find the applicant doing other tasks while being interviewed.',41),(2297,42,167,NULL,166,42,'matching','To pass a phone interview, the most important thing is to answer questions clearly and concisely.',42),(2298,42,167,NULL,166,43,'matching','If you fail to call the interviewer on time, they might not see you as a suitable candidate.',43),(2299,42,167,NULL,166,44,'matching','Applicants should avoid talking about their personal lives if the interviewer has only asked about their professional background and goals.',44),(2300,42,167,NULL,166,45,'matching','It is impolite for an interviewee to interrupt the interviewer in the phone conversation.',45),(2301,42,167,NULL,167,46,'careful_reading','What does the passage tell us about physical disgust?',46),(2302,42,167,NULL,167,47,'careful_reading','How do some researchers perceive moral disgust?',47),(2303,42,167,NULL,167,48,'careful_reading','Why does moral disgust appear quite late in children\'s development?',48),(2304,42,167,NULL,167,49,'careful_reading','What did the author and his colleagues want to examine in their experiment?',49),(2305,42,167,NULL,167,50,'careful_reading','What can we infer about moral disgust from the author and his colleagues\' findings?',50),(2306,42,167,NULL,168,51,'careful_reading','What is the finding of a recent study in Nature?',51),(2307,42,167,NULL,168,52,'careful_reading','What does the passage say about the assumption that social relationships are reciprocal?',52),(2308,42,167,NULL,168,53,'careful_reading','What did Anuj Shah and Michael LaForest want to find out about the belief that social relationships are reciprocal?',53),(2309,42,167,NULL,168,54,'careful_reading','When did Anuj Shah and Michael LaForest find something really interesting in their research?',54),(2310,42,167,NULL,168,55,'careful_reading','What happened in the areas around the housing developments subjected to the studies?',55);
